A||||11||DXR_DAD||injectors rebuilt?||||5||
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||12-27-2001||01:16 PM||||Have any of you had this done?? if so, was there a big improvement? I've seen price from<BR>20 to $30.00per. Is that about right?.<P>And what is it that they do to them?<P><BR>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT GT 87||12-27-2001||08:50 PM||||What is better is to have them blueprinted .They check flow and somehow make them identical . When all your cyl.s are running equal , your engine will be smoother at any rpm , and make more power . I think it's $20 an injector at  <A HREF="http://www.injector.com" TARGET=_blank>www.injector.com</A>      You can use new or old injectors .||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||12-27-2001||09:55 PM||||Yes, that is what I'm talking bout!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rebuild, Blueprinted, Calibrate, flow check??<BR>any of those words?<P>THANKS GT GT<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000003||87GTZ34||12-28-2001||01:16 AM||||DXR,<BR>  They reverse flow a 'cleaning solution' through the injector to remove all the foreign material from inside the injector and on the screen.  Once this is done the injectors are checked at a specific line pressure and have to flow within 2% of each other with a 'good' spray pattern.  If they don't, then the injector is shot and Marren will call you to replace any of the faulty ones.  There is NO tweaking to an injector... They are within spec or not.  Marren does put all new rubber and new 'hats' on them in the service.  The cleaning just lets each injector 'be all it can be' with regard to flow.  When I had mine done, 4 out of the 6 were bad.  The car had 105K on the odometer but the motor had been replaced and only lasted 450 mi after I bought it so I think it had a rough life and probably had more than 105k on it.  Also, they can't do anything for the cold-start injector at all.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pondski||12-28-2001||03:40 AM||||Yep -- he's right! Cleaning and flow check. If they work -- they work! If they don't......time to buy another one.||||reg||14
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||12-28-2001||10:29 AM||||THANKS!!! for the info. Thats what I wanted to hear.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm going to have a set done<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000006||BigTurbo87GT||12-28-2001||11:31 AM||||As a comment on the effect of having it done, it did make a noticable difference on how well my 87 GT ran. Both in idle quality and accelleration. I had 130K on mine when they were done. Marren Motorsports did mine and I'm very happy with their service.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||12-28-2001||01:19 PM||||I sent my injectors to Marren also. They did a good job. Cam back with all new seals, and "hats" and my engine idled and accelerated smoother. Mine had 175K on them when they were done, and they needed it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fie Ro||12-28-2001||04:04 PM||||I had them done last week. They were full of rubbish. two were leaking and one could only flow 26cc, the rest about 36/37cc. They all could be refurbished, they flow 41/42 cc now. I have them in the car and I hope to have it running tomorrow.<P>They should do the testing BEFORE and AFTER cleaning and you should get the results on paper....<P>I paid approx. $180/200 for six. They couldn't test the coldstart injector but I replaced it also. Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fie Ro||12-28-2001||04:14 PM||||I had them done last week. They were full of rubbish. two were leaking and one could only flow 26cc, the rest about 36/37cc. They all could be refurbished, they flow 41/42 cc now. I have them in the car and I hope to have it running tomorrow.<P>They should do the testing BEFORE and AFTER cleaning and you should get the results on paper....<P>I paid approx. $180/200 for six. They couldn't test the coldstart injector but I replaced it also. Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000010||BV MotorSports||12-28-2001||07:27 PM||||I send all my injectors to RC engineering. Very nice work and they come back with the flow test charts and look brand new.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dennis LaGrua||12-30-2001||08:37 PM||||Cleaning fuel injectors can work but at $20 each that's a rip off. You can buy a set of EIGHT BRAND NEW Ford Motorsports fuel injectors for $200 from Summit Racing Equpment in 19, 24 and 36 lb sizes. These injectors will interchange perfectly with the GM units. You would probably have to have a modified engine to use even the 19 lb injectors (stock Fieros are only 15 lb) but you should be able to find similar injecotr buys on a number of other websites.||||reg||13
